IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coq-common`

-- Coroners Act 2003 (Queensland) -- part 3 division 2 (autopsies and the body) as the family meets it, with s 95
-- (authority to bury): concerns about an internal autopsy (s 19(5), (6)), exhumation (s 20(3)-(5)), observing the
-- autopsy (s 21(3)-(5)), asking for a test for an infectious or notifiable condition (s 23A), organs and body parts kept
-- (s 24(4)-(6), (9)), the release of the body (s 26(2)(f), (3), (4)), and burial or cremation (s 95).
--
-- SEAT: a family member of the person who died, or another person with a sufficient interest. See NOTES.md.
--
-- One regulative rule: s 24(6), the coroner's at-most-6-monthly decision whether kept organs or body parts are still
-- needed, run by EVALTRACE inside exported questions that take only plain facts.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Coroners Act 2003: the autopsy and the body`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 19(5), (6) -- my concern about an internal autopsy`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 19(1): "This section does not apply if a coroner-- (a) has stopped investigating a death under section 12(2)(a),
-- (b), (d) or (e); or (b) is investigating a suspected death under section 11(6)." (5): "Before ordering an internal
-- examination of the body, the coroner must, whenever practicable, consider at least the following-- (a) that in some
-- cases a deceased person's family may be distressed by the making of this type of order, for example, because of
-- cultural traditions or spiritual beliefs; (b) any concerns raised by a family member, or another person with a
-- sufficient interest, in relation to the type of examination to be conducted during the autopsy." (6): "If, after
-- considering any concern mentioned in subsection (5)(b), the coroner decides it is still necessary to order the
-- internal examination, the coroner must give a copy of the order to the person who raised the concern."
DECLARE `Kind of autopsy examination` IS ONE OF
    `an examination of cremated remains`
    `an external examination only`
    `an external and partial internal examination`
    `an external and full internal examination`

DECLARE `What must the coroner do about my concern` IS ONE OF
    `s 19 does not apply: the coroner has stopped investigating, or is investigating a suspected death (s 19(1))`
    `s 19(5) does not apply: it applies only before an internal examination is ordered`
    `s 19(5)(b) does not apply: it covers concerns raised by a family member or another person with a sufficient interest`
    `the coroner must, whenever practicable, consider the family's possible distress (s 19(5)(a)); you have raised no concern for s 19(5)(b)`
    `the coroner must, whenever practicable, consider your concern before ordering the internal examination (s 19(5)(b))`
    `the coroner considered your concern and still ordered the internal examination: you must be given a copy of the order (s 19(6))`

GIVEN `s 19 is excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the examination` IS A `Kind of autopsy examination`
      `I am a family member or have a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I raised a concern` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner still ordered it after considering my concern` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What must the coroner do about my concern`
`s 19(5), (6) -- my concern about an internal examination` `s 19 is excluded` `the examination` `I am a family member or have a sufficient interest` `I raised a concern` `the coroner still ordered it after considering my concern` MEANS
    IF `s 19 is excluded`
    THEN `s 19 does not apply: the coroner has stopped investigating, or is investigating a suspected death (s 19(1))`
    ELSE IF NOT `internal`
         THEN `s 19(5) does not apply: it applies only before an internal examination is ordered`
         ELSE IF NOT `I am a family member or have a sufficient interest`
              THEN `s 19(5)(b) does not apply: it covers concerns raised by a family member or another person with a sufficient interest`
              ELSE IF NOT `I raised a concern`
                   THEN `the coroner must, whenever practicable, consider the family's possible distress (s 19(5)(a)); you have raised no concern for s 19(5)(b)`
                   ELSE IF `the coroner still ordered it after considering my concern`
                        THEN `the coroner considered your concern and still ordered the internal examination: you must be given a copy of the order (s 19(6))`
                        ELSE `the coroner must, whenever practicable, consider your concern before ordering the internal examination (s 19(5)(b))`
    WHERE
        `internal` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the examination`
            WHEN `an external and partial internal examination` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an external and full internal examination` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

@export I have a concern about an internal autopsy of the person who died. What must the coroner do about it (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) s 19(5), (6))?
GIVEN `s 19 is excluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the coroner stopped investigating the death (because the remains are Indigenous burial remains, a cause of death certificate is to issue, the State Coroner directed it, or the death is outside the coroner's reach), or is the coroner investigating only a suspected death?
      `the examination` IS A `Kind of autopsy examination` @desc The kind of autopsy examination the coroner is ordering, or has ordered
      `I am a family member or have a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a family member of the person who died, or another person with a sufficient interest in the kind of examination?
      `I raised a concern` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you raised a concern with the coroner about the kind of examination?
      `the coroner still ordered it after considering my concern` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the coroner, after considering your concern, decided an internal examination is still necessary and ordered it?
GIVETH A `What must the coroner do about my concern`
DECIDE `My concern about an internal autopsy question` IS
    `s 19(5), (6) -- my concern about an internal examination` `s 19 is excluded` `the examination` `I am a family member or have a sufficient interest` `I raised a concern` `the coroner still ordered it after considering my concern`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 20(3)-(5) -- notice before an exhumation`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 20(3): "The State Coroner must give at least 2 days notice of the State Coroner's intention to make the order to--
-- (a) the person in charge of the place where the body is, or the cremated remains are; and (b) any person who the
-- State Coroner considers has a sufficient interest in the autopsy." (4): "Subsection (3) does not apply if-- (a) after
-- taking all reasonable steps, the State Coroner can not contact a person mentioned in subsection (3); or (b) the State
-- Coroner considers it is not, in the circumstances, in the public interest to notify a person". (5): if a person has
-- raised a concern but, after discussing it with them, the State Coroner considers the order in the public interest, "the
-- State Coroner must make the order and give a copy of it to the person."
DECLARE `Must I be told before an exhumation` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the State Coroner must give you at least 2 days notice of the intended order (s 20(3)); if you raise a concern and, after discussing it with you, the State Coroner still considers the order in the public interest, you must be given a copy of the order (s 20(5))`
    `no: s 20(3) does not apply, as the State Coroner could not contact you after taking all reasonable steps (s 20(4)(a))`
    `no: s 20(3) does not apply, as the State Coroner considers notifying you is not in the public interest (s 20(4)(b))`
    `no: s 20(3) requires notice only to the person in charge of the place and to persons the State Coroner considers have a sufficient interest in the autopsy`

GIVEN `I am in charge of the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State Coroner considers I have a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I could not be contacted after all reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State Coroner considers notice not in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Must I be told before an exhumation`
`s 20(3), (4) -- notice of an exhumation` `I am in charge of the place` `the State Coroner considers I have a sufficient interest` `I could not be contacted after all reasonable steps` `the State Coroner considers notice not in the public interest` MEANS
    IF NOT (`I am in charge of the place` OR `the State Coroner considers I have a sufficient interest`)
    THEN `no: s 20(3) requires notice only to the person in charge of the place and to persons the State Coroner considers have a sufficient interest in the autopsy`
    ELSE IF `I could not be contacted after all reasonable steps`
         THEN `no: s 20(3) does not apply, as the State Coroner could not contact you after taking all reasonable steps (s 20(4)(a))`
         ELSE IF `the State Coroner considers notice not in the public interest`
              THEN `no: s 20(3) does not apply, as the State Coroner considers notifying you is not in the public interest (s 20(4)(b))`
              ELSE `yes: the State Coroner must give you at least 2 days notice of the intended order (s 20(3)); if you raise a concern and, after discussing it with you, the State Coroner still considers the order in the public interest, you must be given a copy of the order (s 20(5))`

@export The State Coroner may order the body exhumed, or the cremated remains recovered, for an autopsy. Must I be told first (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) s 20(3)-(5))?
GIVEN `I am in charge of the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person in charge of the place where the body or cremated remains are (for example a cemetery)?
      `the State Coroner considers I have a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the State Coroner consider you have a sufficient interest in the autopsy (a close relative usually will)?
      `I could not be contacted after all reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the State Coroner been unable to contact you after taking all reasonable steps?
      `the State Coroner considers notice not in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the State Coroner consider that, in the circumstances, notifying you is not in the public interest?
GIVETH A `Must I be told before an exhumation`
DECIDE `Must I be told before an exhumation question` IS
    `s 20(3), (4) -- notice of an exhumation` `I am in charge of the place` `the State Coroner considers I have a sufficient interest` `I could not be contacted after all reasonable steps` `the State Coroner considers notice not in the public interest`

-- "At least 2 days notice": the order may be made on the notice day plus 2 (fork F6: or plus 3, if the 2 days are clear
-- days).
@export I was given notice of an intended exhumation order. From what day may the State Coroner make the order (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) s 20(3))?
GIVEN `the day I was given notice` IS A DATE @desc The date you were given notice of the State Coroner's intention to make the order (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Earliest day for the exhumation order question` IS 2 `days after` `the day I was given notice`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 21(3)-(5) -- observing the autopsy`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 21(3): "The coroner may allow a person, or the person's representative, to observe the autopsy if the coroner
-- considers-- (a) the person has a sufficient interest in the autopsy; and (b) the attendance ... would not compromise
-- the integrity of the coronial investigation or any other investigation into the death; and (c) the attendance ... is
-- otherwise appropriate." (4): before allowing it the coroner must, whenever practicable, consult a family member and the
-- doctor. (5): "If the coroner allows a person to observe an autopsy under subsection (3), the coroner must give the
-- person notice of the time and place of the autopsy before it is conducted."
DECLARE `Can I observe the autopsy` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the coroner has allowed you, or your representative, to observe; you must be given notice of the time and place before the autopsy (s 21(3), (5))`
    `possibly: the coroner may allow you, or your representative, to observe (s 21(3)), after consulting a family member and the doctor whenever practicable (s 21(4))`
    `no: s 21(3) does not let the coroner allow it unless the coroner considers you have a sufficient interest, your attendance would not compromise any investigation, and it is otherwise appropriate`

GIVEN `the coroner considers I have a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner considers attendance would not compromise an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner considers attendance otherwise appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner has allowed me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can I observe the autopsy`
`s 21(3)-(5) -- observing the autopsy` `the coroner considers I have a sufficient interest` `the coroner considers attendance would not compromise an investigation` `the coroner considers attendance otherwise appropriate` `the coroner has allowed me` MEANS
    IF `the coroner considers I have a sufficient interest` AND `the coroner considers attendance would not compromise an investigation` AND `the coroner considers attendance otherwise appropriate`
    THEN IF `the coroner has allowed me`
         THEN `yes: the coroner has allowed you, or your representative, to observe; you must be given notice of the time and place before the autopsy (s 21(3), (5))`
         ELSE `possibly: the coroner may allow you, or your representative, to observe (s 21(3)), after consulting a family member and the doctor whenever practicable (s 21(4))`
    ELSE `no: s 21(3) does not let the coroner allow it unless the coroner considers you have a sufficient interest, your attendance would not compromise any investigation, and it is otherwise appropriate`

@export Can I, or my representative, observe the autopsy (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) s 21(3)-(5))?
GIVEN `the coroner considers I have a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the coroner consider you have a sufficient interest in the autopsy?
      `the coroner considers attendance would not compromise an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the coroner consider your attendance would not compromise the coronial investigation or any other investigation (criminal, workplace safety, disciplinary)?
      `the coroner considers attendance otherwise appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the coroner consider your attendance otherwise appropriate?
      `the coroner has allowed me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the coroner allowed you to observe?
GIVETH A `Can I observe the autopsy`
DECIDE `Can I observe the autopsy question` IS
    `s 21(3)-(5) -- observing the autopsy` `the coroner considers I have a sufficient interest` `the coroner considers attendance would not compromise an investigation` `the coroner considers attendance otherwise appropriate` `the coroner has allowed me`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 23A -- asking for a test for an infectious or notifiable condition`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 23A(1): "A person may apply to the coroner in writing for an order that the doctor ... also conduct a test for any
-- or all of the following as stated in the application-- (a) an infectious condition; (b) a notifiable condition; (c) an
-- emergency notifiable condition; (d) a controlled notifiable condition." (2): "The coroner may grant the application
-- only if the coroner is satisfied the applicant has a sufficient interest in the test result." The conditions are
-- Public Health Act 2005 terms, asked as a fact. s 52(1)(c)(i): the applicant may have access to the result.
DECLARE `The test I want` IS ONE OF
    `a test for an infectious, notifiable, emergency notifiable or controlled notifiable condition`
    `another test`

DECLARE `Can I get the autopsy test` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you may apply in writing and the coroner may order the test (s 23A(1), (2)); you may then have access to the result (s 52(1)(c)(i))`
    `no: the coroner may grant the application only if satisfied you have a sufficient interest in the test result (s 23A(2))`
    `not under s 23A, which covers only tests for infectious and notifiable conditions; the coroner may still order a test on the coroner's own initiative (s 23(2))`

GIVEN `the test` IS A `The test I want`
      `the coroner is satisfied I have a sufficient interest in the result` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can I get the autopsy test`
`s 23A -- applying for an autopsy test` `the test` `the coroner is satisfied I have a sufficient interest in the result` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the test`
    WHEN `another test` THEN `not under s 23A, which covers only tests for infectious and notifiable conditions; the coroner may still order a test on the coroner's own initiative (s 23(2))`
    WHEN `a test for an infectious, notifiable, emergency notifiable or controlled notifiable condition` THEN
        IF `the coroner is satisfied I have a sufficient interest in the result`
        THEN `yes: you may apply in writing and the coroner may order the test (s 23A(1), (2)); you may then have access to the result (s 52(1)(c)(i))`
        ELSE `no: the coroner may grant the application only if satisfied you have a sufficient interest in the test result (s 23A(2))`

@export Can I ask the coroner to have the body tested for an infectious or notifiable disease, for example because I was exposed (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) s 23A)?
GIVEN `the test` IS A `The test I want` @desc The test you want done
      `the coroner is satisfied I have a sufficient interest in the result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the coroner satisfied you have a sufficient interest in the test result (for example you may have been exposed to the condition)?
GIVETH A `Can I get the autopsy test`
DECIDE `Can I get an autopsy test question` IS
    `s 23A -- applying for an autopsy test` `the test` `the coroner is satisfied I have a sufficient interest in the result`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 24(4), (5), 26(2)(f), (3), (4) -- the release of the body after the autopsy`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 26(2): the coroner stops having control of the body when the coroner "(f) decides that it is not necessary for the
-- coroner's investigation to keep the body after an autopsy and the coroner orders the release of the body for burial."
-- (3): "For subsection (2)(f), the coroner must order the release of the body for burial as soon as reasonably
-- practicable after the autopsy." (4): "However, the coroner must not order the release of a body for burial if it is
-- not known whose body it is, unless the coroner believes it is necessary to bury the body in the particular
-- circumstances." s 24(4): if prescribed tissue (a whole organ or fetus, or an identifiable body part) has been removed,
-- the coroner "must not order the release of the body unless satisfied that-- (a) if practicable, a family member ...
-- has been informed of the removal ...; and (b) the retention ... is necessary for the investigation of the death,
-- despite any concerns raised". (5): if not so satisfied, "the coroner must order the doctor to return the prescribed
-- tissue to the body before the body is released." "As soon as reasonably practicable" has no number of days (no WITHIN).
-- The release on the other paths of s 26(2)(a)-(e) is out of scope (NOTES.md).
DECLARE `Will the body be released` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the coroner must order the release of the body for burial as soon as reasonably practicable after the autopsy (s 26(2)(f), (3))`
    `yes, with the organs or body parts kept returned to it: the coroner is not satisfied of s 24(4)(a) and (b), so must order the doctor to return them to the body before it is released (s 24(5)); and must order the release as soon as reasonably practicable (s 26(3))`
    `yes, without the organs or body parts kept: a family member has been told (if practicable) and the coroner is satisfied keeping them is necessary (s 24(4)); the coroner must order the release as soon as reasonably practicable (s 26(3)) and review the kept tissue at most every 6 months (s 24(6))`
    `not yet: the coroner keeps control of the body until deciding it is no longer needed for the investigation (s 26(2)(f))`
    `no: the coroner must not order the release for burial while it is not known whose body it is, unless the coroner believes burial is necessary (s 26(4))`
    `not covered: this question covers the release after an autopsy (s 26(2)(f)); the other paths of s 26(2) are not encoded`

GIVEN `an autopsy has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner decided the body is no longer needed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is known whose body it is` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner believes burial is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `prescribed tissue was removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a family member was told of the removal or it was not practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner is satisfied keeping the tissue is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Will the body be released`
`ss 24(4), (5), 26(2)(f), (3), (4) -- release after the autopsy` `an autopsy has been done` `the coroner decided the body is no longer needed` `it is known whose body it is` `the coroner believes burial is necessary` `prescribed tissue was removed` `a family member was told of the removal or it was not practicable` `the coroner is satisfied keeping the tissue is necessary` MEANS
    IF NOT `an autopsy has been done`
    THEN `not covered: this question covers the release after an autopsy (s 26(2)(f)); the other paths of s 26(2) are not encoded`
    ELSE IF NOT `the coroner decided the body is no longer needed`
         THEN `not yet: the coroner keeps control of the body until deciding it is no longer needed for the investigation (s 26(2)(f))`
         ELSE IF (NOT `it is known whose body it is`) AND (NOT `the coroner believes burial is necessary`)
              THEN `no: the coroner must not order the release for burial while it is not known whose body it is, unless the coroner believes burial is necessary (s 26(4))`
              ELSE IF NOT `prescribed tissue was removed`
                   THEN `yes: the coroner must order the release of the body for burial as soon as reasonably practicable after the autopsy (s 26(2)(f), (3))`
                   ELSE IF `a family member was told of the removal or it was not practicable` AND `the coroner is satisfied keeping the tissue is necessary`
                        THEN `yes, without the organs or body parts kept: a family member has been told (if practicable) and the coroner is satisfied keeping them is necessary (s 24(4)); the coroner must order the release as soon as reasonably practicable (s 26(3)) and review the kept tissue at most every 6 months (s 24(6))`
                        ELSE `yes, with the organs or body parts kept returned to it: the coroner is not satisfied of s 24(4)(a) and (b), so must order the doctor to return them to the body before it is released (s 24(5)); and must order the release as soon as reasonably practicable (s 26(3))`

@export The autopsy is done. Will the body be released to us for burial or cremation, and with or without any organs or body parts kept (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) ss 24(4), (5) and 26)?
GIVEN `an autopsy has been done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the autopsy been done?
      `the coroner decided the body is no longer needed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the coroner decided it is not necessary for the investigation to keep the body?
      `it is known whose body it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it known whose body it is?
      `the coroner believes burial is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is not known whose body it is: does the coroner believe it is necessary to bury the body in the circumstances?
      `prescribed tissue was removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the doctor remove a whole organ, a fetus, or an identifiable body part (such as a limb, digit or jaw) for testing?
      `a family member was told of the removal or it was not practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the coroner satisfied that a family member has been told of the removal, or that telling one was not practicable?
      `the coroner is satisfied keeping the tissue is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the coroner satisfied that keeping the organ or body part is necessary for the investigation, despite any concerns raised?
GIVETH A `Will the body be released`
DECIDE `Will the body be released question` IS
    `ss 24(4), (5), 26(2)(f), (3), (4) -- release after the autopsy` `an autopsy has been done` `the coroner decided the body is no longer needed` `it is known whose body it is` `the coroner believes burial is necessary` `prescribed tissue was removed` `a family member was told of the removal or it was not practicable` `the coroner is satisfied keeping the tissue is necessary`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 24(6) -- the 6-monthly review of organs or body parts kept`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 24(6): "If tissue kept for testing is prescribed tissue, the coroner must, at not more than 6-monthly intervals after
-- the date of the order for the autopsy, decide whether the tissue-- (a) still needs to be kept for-- (i) the
-- investigation of the death; or (ii) proceedings for an offence relating to the death; or (b) may be disposed of."
-- Read as: each decision within 6 months after the order (for the first) or after the last decision (fork F7: or on
-- fixed 6-monthly anniversaries of the order). The rule counts in days from the day the interval starts.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Coronial party` `Coronial act`
`s 24(6) -- decide on the kept tissue within the interval` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the coroner`
    MUST `decide whether the prescribed tissue still needs to be kept`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the coroner` BECAUSE "s 24(6): the coroner did not decide, within 6 months after the autopsy order or the last decision, whether the kept organ or body part still needs to be kept"

GIVEN `the day the interval starts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 24(6) -- the last day of the interval` `the day the interval starts` MEANS 6 `months after` `the day the interval starts`

@export Organs or body parts from the autopsy are being kept. By what day must the coroner next decide whether they still need to be kept (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) s 24(6))?
GIVEN `the day the interval starts` IS A DATE @desc The date of the autopsy order, or of the coroner's last decision about keeping the tissue if there has been one (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Last day for the tissue decision question` IS
    `s 24(6) -- the last day of the interval` `the day the interval starts`

@export Organs or body parts from the autopsy are being kept. Has the coroner decided in time whether they still need to be kept (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) s 24(6))?
GIVEN `the day the interval starts` IS A DATE @desc The date of the autopsy order, or of the coroner's last decision about keeping the tissue if there has been one (ISO 8601)
      `the coroner has decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the coroner since made the decision whether the tissue still needs to be kept?
      `the day the coroner decided` IS A DATE @desc The date the coroner decided (ISO 8601); if not yet, any date
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date (ISO 8601)
GIVETH AN `Is the coroner's step in time`
DECIDE `Tissue decision in time question` IS
    `the state of` `decide whether the prescribed tissue still needs to be kept` `under` (`s 24(6) -- decide on the kept tissue within the interval` (`the number of days from` `the day the interval starts` `until` (`s 24(6) -- the last day of the interval` `the day the interval starts`))) `from` `the day the interval starts` `done` `the coroner has decided` `on` `the day the coroner decided` `as at` `today`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 24(7)-(9) -- organs or body parts when the coroner orders disposal`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 24(7): specimen tissue (Transplantation and Anatomy Act 1979) "must be kept indefinitely". (8): other tissue must
-- not be disposed of except under a coroner's order. (9): "If a coroner orders the disposal of the tissue, the entity
-- that has the tissue must-- (a) if a family member of the deceased person has told the coroner that he or she wishes to
-- test, or use, the tissue for a lawful purpose or to bury the tissue--release the tissue to the family member, or the
-- family member's representative, for the test, use or burial; or (b) otherwise--arrange for the tissue to be buried."
DECLARE `What happens to the kept tissue` IS ONE OF
    `it must be released to you, or your representative, for the test, use or burial you told the coroner of (s 24(9)(a))`
    `it must be buried, as no family member has told the coroner of a wish to test, use or bury it (s 24(9)(b))`
    `it must be kept indefinitely: it has been made into specimen tissue (s 24(7))`
    `it must be kept: it must not be disposed of except under a coroner's order (s 24(8))`

GIVEN `it is specimen tissue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner has ordered its disposal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a family member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I told the coroner I wish to test, use or bury it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What happens to the kept tissue`
`s 24(7)-(9) -- the kept tissue` `it is specimen tissue` `the coroner has ordered its disposal` `I am a family member` `I told the coroner I wish to test, use or bury it` MEANS
    IF `it is specimen tissue`
    THEN `it must be kept indefinitely: it has been made into specimen tissue (s 24(7))`
    ELSE IF NOT `the coroner has ordered its disposal`
         THEN `it must be kept: it must not be disposed of except under a coroner's order (s 24(8))`
         ELSE IF `I am a family member` AND `I told the coroner I wish to test, use or bury it`
              THEN `it must be released to you, or your representative, for the test, use or burial you told the coroner of (s 24(9)(a))`
              ELSE `it must be buried, as no family member has told the coroner of a wish to test, use or bury it (s 24(9)(b))`

@export What happens to the organs, body parts or other tissue kept from the autopsy? Can they be released to me (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) s 24(7)-(9))?
GIVEN `it is specimen tissue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the tissue been made into specimen tissue under the Transplantation and Anatomy Act 1979 (for example a preserved slide or block)?
      `the coroner has ordered its disposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a coroner ordered the disposal of the tissue?
      `I am a family member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the family member of the person who died, for the Coroners Act?
      `I told the coroner I wish to test, use or bury it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you told the coroner you wish to test or use the tissue for a lawful purpose, or to bury it?
GIVETH A `What happens to the kept tissue`
DECIDE `What happens to the kept tissue question` IS
    `s 24(7)-(9) -- the kept tissue` `it is specimen tissue` `the coroner has ordered its disposal` `I am a family member` `I told the coroner I wish to test, use or bury it`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 95 -- may we bury or cremate the body, or take it out of Queensland`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 95(1): "A person must not-- (a) prepare a human body for burial; or (b) bury a human body; or (c) take a human body
-- out of Queensland; unless the person is authorised to do so under subsection (2). Maximum penalty--120 penalty units."
-- (2): "A person is authorised if-- (a) for a death investigated by a coroner-- (i) a certificate of the cause of death
-- ... has been issued with the coroner's consent; or (ii) the coroner has ordered the release of the body under section
-- 26; or (b) for a death investigated by a non-Queensland coroner--a non-Queensland coroner's release certificate has
-- been issued; or (c) otherwise--a cause of death certificate has been issued." Sch 2: "burial includes cremation or
-- other lawful disposal". A flat "must not ... unless": when no head of (2) holds, the answer is no.
DECLARE `Who is investigating the death` IS ONE OF
    `a Queensland coroner`
    `a coroner outside Queensland`
    `no coroner`

DECLARE `May we bury the body` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you are authorised, as a cause of death certificate has been issued with the coroner's consent (s 95(2)(a)(i))`
    `yes: you are authorised, as the coroner has ordered the release of the body (s 95(2)(a)(ii))`
    `yes: you are authorised, as a non-Queensland coroner's release certificate has been issued (s 95(2)(b))`
    `yes: you are authorised, as a cause of death certificate has been issued (s 95(2)(c))`
    `no: you must not prepare the body for burial, bury or cremate it, or take it out of Queensland until authorised under s 95(2); maximum penalty 120 penalty units (s 95(1))`

GIVEN `who is investigating` IS A `Who is investigating the death`
      `a cause of death certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner consented to the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coroner ordered the release of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a non-Queensland release certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `May we bury the body`
`s 95 -- authority to bury` `who is investigating` `a cause of death certificate has been issued` `the coroner consented to the certificate` `the coroner ordered the release of the body` `a non-Queensland release certificate has been issued` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who is investigating`
    WHEN `a Queensland coroner` THEN
        IF `a cause of death certificate has been issued` AND `the coroner consented to the certificate`
        THEN `yes: you are authorised, as a cause of death certificate has been issued with the coroner's consent (s 95(2)(a)(i))`
        ELSE IF `the coroner ordered the release of the body`
             THEN `yes: you are authorised, as the coroner has ordered the release of the body (s 95(2)(a)(ii))`
             ELSE `no: you must not prepare the body for burial, bury or cremate it, or take it out of Queensland until authorised under s 95(2); maximum penalty 120 penalty units (s 95(1))`
    WHEN `a coroner outside Queensland` THEN
        IF `a non-Queensland release certificate has been issued`
        THEN `yes: you are authorised, as a non-Queensland coroner's release certificate has been issued (s 95(2)(b))`
        ELSE `no: you must not prepare the body for burial, bury or cremate it, or take it out of Queensland until authorised under s 95(2); maximum penalty 120 penalty units (s 95(1))`
    WHEN `no coroner` THEN
        IF `a cause of death certificate has been issued`
        THEN `yes: you are authorised, as a cause of death certificate has been issued (s 95(2)(c))`
        ELSE `no: you must not prepare the body for burial, bury or cremate it, or take it out of Queensland until authorised under s 95(2); maximum penalty 120 penalty units (s 95(1))`

@export May we prepare the body for burial, bury or cremate it, or take it out of Queensland (Coroners Act 2003 (Qld) s 95)?
GIVEN `who is investigating` IS A `Who is investigating the death` @desc Whether a coroner in Queensland, a coroner elsewhere, or no coroner is investigating the death
      `a cause of death certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a doctor issued a cause of death certificate?
      `the coroner consented to the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a Queensland coroner is investigating: was the certificate issued with the coroner's consent?
      `the coroner ordered the release of the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a Queensland coroner is investigating: has the coroner ordered the release of the body?
      `a non-Queensland release certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a coroner outside Queensland is investigating: has that coroner issued a certificate releasing the body?
GIVETH A `May we bury the body`
DECIDE `May we bury the body question` IS
    `s 95 -- authority to bury` `who is investigating` `a cause of death certificate has been issued` `the coroner consented to the certificate` `the coroner ordered the release of the body` `a non-Queensland release certificate has been issued`
